Steve Leferve wrote:
>
> What are the most valuable rings? Is there a difference between rings you
> value in the early game and rings you value in the late game?

In the early game, the valuable rings are the ones that grant
important resistance intrinsics that you haven't gotten from
corpses yet.  Poison, electricity, cold, fire.  But enough
corpses grant these that by the middle game they become only
usefull as polypile fodder.

In the late game I like searching and free action to keep on
much of the time, with conflict, levitation and slow digestion
to keep in reserve as needed.

In the end game on the way back up with the amulet, free action,
conflict and slow digestion become very important with levitation
in reserve.  With 3 important rings and 2 ring fingers, it's the
usual NetHack situtation of having several correct answers.

The chargable rings, I don't find them all that usefull.
Adornment can be fixed with enough blessed !oIA.  Increase
accuracy and damage can be fixed with a luckstone or ?oEW.
Protection can be gotten via prayer or donation.  Basically
okay in the early game then progressively less so.

Polymorph and polymorph control is critical for one class, good
for some playing styles, and pointless for otehr playing styles.

